    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature for pet owners end-to-end, following the existing Spring/OpenAPI conventions in this codebase (derived fields are computed on the `Owner` entity and surfaced via the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, with input/output fields declared in `openapi.yml` from which the DTOs are generated).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**\n   - Added an optional `title` input field to the `OwnerFields` schema (string, documented as `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`) \u2014 stored and returned.\n   - Added a read-only `salutation` derived field to the `Owner` schema.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`**\n   - Added the `title` column (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter.\n   - Added `getSalutation()`: returns `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**\n   - Mapped `salutation` via `owner.getSalutation()` in `toOwnerDto`. (`title` maps automatically by name on both read and write.)\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)\n   - Added the `title` column to the `owners` table. Seed-data inserts use explicit column lists, so they were unaffected.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreComposesSalutation` passes (posting `title=DR`, `lastName=who` yields `salutation` = `\"DR who\"`), and the full suite builds green.",
