    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change mirrors the existing conventions of this codebase cleanly:\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `getSalutation()` is a derived read-only property composed from other `Owner` fields, so placing it as a computed getter on the `Owner` domain model is the natural home \u2014 exactly where `getInitials()` already lives.\n- **Mapper follows the established pattern.** The new `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(owner.getSalutation())\")` is a direct analog of the pre-existing `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(owner.getInitials())\")` line right above it. A maintainer would find this immediately familiar; the mapper correctly delegates the composition to the model rather than embedding the null/blank logic inline.\n- **No duplication / no catch-all.** The title/null branching lives in one place; the mapper, DTO, and schema just carry the field through. `Owner` isn't being turned into a dumping ground \u2014 this is the same shape of member it already hosts.\n- **Supporting changes are consistent and additive.** The `title` column, its getter/setter, the four DB schema variants, and the OpenAPI `title` (writable) + `salutation` (readOnly) entries are all idiomatic and match how sibling fields are declared.\n\nNo structural improvements needed.",
